From c3146a10def4c452e2e8caab5c884ca7750c9a2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Mutai <official.daniel.mutai@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 09:50:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(inventory): shared product catalog + label OCR scanning

Two related additions:

1. Shared cross-org product catalog
   - New ProductCatalogEntry model (barcode unique, name/brand/category/
     unit/imageUrl, source MANUAL|OCR|OPEN_FOOD_FACTS, confirmations
     counter). Deliberately has no relation to Organization - it's
     anonymous aggregate knowledge (barcode -> product), not per-org data.
   - lookupExternalProduct() now checks the catalog before Open Food
     Facts, and seeds the catalog whenever Open Food Facts resolves a
     barcode for the first time.
   - create() now contributes every barcode+name it creates back into
     the catalog (fire-and-forget, never blocks the actual save). This
     is what makes it improve over time: a barcode manually entered (or
     OCR-confirmed) by one org becomes an instant match for any other
     org that scans it later, addressing the coverage gap general
     product databases have for local/regional goods.
   - Migration written by hand (prisma generate can't reach
     binaries.prisma.sh from this sandbox - pre-existing limitation,
     see prior commits); matches the project's existing migration.sql
     format exactly.

2. Label/packaging OCR scanning
   - expiryDate/batchNumber (already on the InventoryItem Prisma model,
     never wired up) are now accepted end-to-end: DTO -> service
     (server-side date validation, so a malformed date can't reach the
     DB) -> AddItemSheet form fields.
   - New LABEL_OCR source mode on the existing ai-ingestion parser
     (reuses the same engine that already turns receipt OCR text into
     structured actions - no new AI plumbing). Extracts one CREATE
     action per label photo: name, category, unit, and, if present,
     expiry/batch via the same metadata.expiryDate/batchNumber
     convention the CHEMIST prompt already uses.
   - New useLabelOcrCapture hook: triggers the device camera (same
     capture="environment" file-input pattern the existing receipt
     upload flow uses), uploads to the existing /ocr/receipt text
     extraction endpoint, feeds the result through LABEL_OCR parsing,
     and normalizes/validates any extracted date before it's usable
     (defends against the AI returning an unparseable or implausible
     date - reachable defense-in-depth also added server-side).
   - Two entry points, sharing the same hook: a "Scan Label" button
     inside AddItemSheet (fills the currently-open form), and a new
     mode picker on TopBar's scan button ("Scan Barcode" vs "Scan
     Label/Packaging") for starting fresh - since TopBar is global and
     has no direct access to the inventory page's state, that path
     hands off via a short-lived sessionStorage key
     (OCR_DRAFT_STORAGE_KEY) read once by the inventory page.
   - All prefills (catalog/Open Food Facts and OCR) are strictly
     non-destructive: existing user input is never overwritten, and a
     failed/empty lookup just leaves manual entry as today's fallback.

Verified with tsc --noEmit on the frontend workspace (0 errors).
Backend changes reviewed manually, not tsc-verified - Prisma engine
binaries are blocked by this sandbox's network policy (pre-existing,
unrelated to this change); mirrors established patterns exactly
(fetch() like ocr.service.ts, Prisma calls like existing service
methods, migration.sql format matching prior migrations byte-for-byte
in structure).
